   161	    """
   162	    Pour the hanging droplet into a bottom-connected multi-chamber vessel and fill all cavity cells below the common waterline.
   163	
   164	    Input structure:
   165	    - A grey wall structure sits on a black background and forms one container with several upward-open vertical chambers.
   166	    - The chambers are connected through lower internal passages, and some chambers contain bottom protrusions or steps.
   167	    - Exactly one connected colored droplet hangs above one chamber mouth; its pixel count is the water volume.
   168	
   169	    Rule:
   170	    - Count the droplet pixels to get volume n.
   171	    - Identify the connected inner cavity reachable from the chamber mouths inside the wall bounding box.
   172	    - Choose the unique horizontal level whose strictly-below cavity cells total exactly n, erase the droplet, and recolor those cavity cells with the droplet color.
   173	
   174	    Key insight:
   175	    - The droplet does not stay in its source chamber: bottom connectivity forces one shared waterline, so the answer is determined jointly by volume conservation and a global equal-height fill across all chambers.
   176	    """
   177	    info = _parse_scene(np.asarray(grid, dtype=int))
   178	    g = info["grid"]
   179	    bg = int(info["bg"])
   180	    water_color = int(info["water_color"])
   181	    volume = int(info["droplet_mask"].sum())
   182	    fill_mask = _fill_mask_for_volume(info["cavity_mask"], volume)
   183	
   184	    out = g.copy()
